four badge ideas/code paths reused from the fork kesemb2/Pictorium-HE
(https://github.com/kesemb2/Pictorium-HE) at pinned commit
9bbd83961d2d9cc368c9ec21efd9bda927a2e292 (source verified 2026-10-20):
1. exact TMDB keyword matching for "based on (a) true story" and the
   "based on novel or book" variants (tag-catalog.ts KEYWORD_TAGS
   s_truestory/s_book) — only these two entries;
2. "Only N episodes" enrichment for miniseries with a known episode
   count of 1..8 (tag-catalog.ts fewEpisodes);
3. future next-episode label within 14 days (poster-badge.ts
   getNextEpisodeLabel);
4. its priority placement right after the new-season badge
   (badge-priority.ts, `new` bucket).
Daily tag rotation, trending/highly-rated badges and every other fork tag
were deliberately NOT reused. All surrounding integration (calendar-day
window, 18-locale keys, ephemeral cache lifetime, editor wiring) is
original work, not fork-attributed.

Anime filler classification snapshot (CC BY 4.0)
------------------------------------------------
The bundled file src/generated/anime-filler-map.json is derived from
"anime-filler-list-data" by animecannonhunter-hash:
  https://github.com/animecannonhunter-hash/anime-filler-list-data
Pinned revision a7b28ff590b70652843125b77b9a80f334d2c3ca
(snapshot date 2026-08-19), licensed under CC BY 4.0:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Source site: https://skipthefiller.com

Changes made by this project: only per-episode manga canon/anime canon/
filler/mixed classification codes were extracted and compressed into absolute
episode ranges; aggregate counts were recomputed from episode rows;
anime that could not be mapped to a single TMDB target are excluded
and listed in the snapshot meta.skipped. Legacy v1 snapshots (single `canon`
code) are still read with `canon` normalized to `manga`.

